Kamikaze Kitty (kkitty@netcom.com) wrote:
: I'm trying to setup NetHack on my g/f's Amiga 1200's HD. Not being 
: completely familiar with the Amiga, I ran into a bit of trouble getting 
: it configured to work off of the HD.  It works great off of floppy, but I 
: have no idea what I should set the various things in the config.  Right 
: now there are three directories on WORK: NetHack, HackExe, HackExe2 
: corisponding to which floppy the files should be on.
:   
:    Any help would be very much appreciated...

All the help you need should be in the verbose help files on the subject; at
the very least the Read Me file in the NetHack disk/directory.

basically you should create a nethack directory NH313 on a partition on theHD,
then in this dir makedir NetHack , makedir HackExe and makedir HackExe2.
then assign NetHack:,HackExe:,and HackExe2: to the above directories
 (eg assign NetHack: Games:NH313/NetHack )
 then unarchive the files in the correct directories,and edit the NetHack.cnf
file thus : 
      	HACKDIR=NetHack:
	LEVELS=NetHack:levels
	SAVE=NetHack:save;n (n means dont prompt for save disk--this is a HD)
	PATH=NetHack:;HackExe:

If you have set everything up right,this prolly should work. Otherwise go 
back to the help files. If you get really stuck,ftp the archived files off
any aminet site (eg ftp.wustl.edu or ftp.cdrom.com ) and use these files to 
set it up on your system.

Hope this helps,dood. Have fun with your gf's ami ;) *wink*

